# UI.NextJs.Framework Architecture

Next.js 15 App Router app mirroring Unity.UI.Framework layout and patterns in React.

## Framework-first

Always use shared framework primitives before building custom UI, state, or API layers:

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Buttons, typography, layout, callouts, icons, badges | `@design-system` |
| List / search UI | `@entity-framework` (`EntityGrid`, search + grid hooks) |
| Create/edit form from server JSON Schema | `@json-schema-form` (`JsonSchemaForm`, `useJsonSchemaEntityForm`) |
| Routed feature modals (create / edit forms only) | `@design-system` `RoutedModal` + App Router `@modal` parallel route |
| API HTTP | `systemApiFetch` from `@/framework/api/system-api-fetch` |
| Auth session | `@auth/*` (`useAuth`, sign-in) |

Prefer extending `src/framework/` over one-off feature reimplementations.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/config/` | `environment.ts`, `api-routes.ts`, `api-url.ts` |
| `src/framework/design-system/` | Component library |
| `src/framework/entity-framework/` | Grids, search, entity providers |
| `src/framework/json-schema-form/` | Schema forms + client validation against server schema |
| `src/framework/api/` | `systemApiFetch` |
| `src/framework/auth/` | Auth provider / tokens |
| `src/features/` | Product features (thin wiring) |
| `src/app/` | Next.js routes, layouts, parallel `@modal` slots |
| `src/shell/` | Chrome such as `SiteNav` |

## Path aliases

Import via aliases from `tsconfig.json`: `@design-system`, `@entity-framework`, `@json-schema-form`, `@auth/*`, `@shell/*`, `@features/*`, `@/*`.

## API configuration

- All API calls go to the System API (API.Framework, versionless routes, no `/v1`) URLs built from `environment.apiRoot` via `apiRoutes` in `src/config/api-routes.ts`.
- `environment.apiRoot` reads `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SYSTEM_API_ROOT` (Neil sets this in `.env.local`).
- **Never open, create, or edit any `.env*` file. Never change the default string in `src/config/environment.ts`.**
- `NEXT_PUBLIC_SYSTEM_APP_ID` is likewise owned by Neil in `.env.local`.
- Centralize paths in `apiRoutes` — do not hardcode API URLs in features.

## Feature activation

1. Implement under `src/features/{area}/`
2. Add routes under `src/app/...` that render feature components
3. List pages render filters + results on the route itself; add parallel `@modal` intercepting routes only for create / edit forms (copy `examples/animals`; see `nextjs-list-pages.mdc`)

## Component defaults

- Design-system first (see `style/nextjs-design-system.mdc`)
- Interactive roots: `'use client'`
- `tid` on interactive elements
- Single quotes, 2-space indent (see formatting rule)

## Before implementing

1. Read `src/framework/design-system/README.md` and `src/framework/README.md`
2. Copy **reference-data** and/or **animals** feature slices — do not invent a parallel architecture
3. Follow focused rules under `.cursor/rules/framework/` for grids, forms, modals, and state
